<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romani people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Roma, Romani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Romani people, or Roma, are an ethnic group whose ancestors left north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around a thousand years ago and reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> by the 14th century. Long subject to discrimination, enslavement in Wallachia and Moldavia, and expulsions, they were targeted for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and its allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, when hundreds of thousands were murdered. They are Europe's largest ethnic minority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romani-people.jpg" alt="Romani people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AdiJapan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Romani_people.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
